\begin{frame}{Literature on racializing discourse}
  A framework previously applied to African-Americans (AAs) \smallcite{myers_race_2001}:
  \begin{itemize}
    \item \alert{Boundary marking}: Creating and characterizing categories
    \begin{itemize}
      \item Racial slurs, caricatures, dehumanizing anything associated with AAs
    \end{itemize}
    \item \alert{Boundary policing}: Denying others access to one's group's boundaries
    \begin{itemize}
      \item Carried out by White people
    \end{itemize}
    \item \alert{Boundary maintaining}: Denying members of one's group access to others' boundaries
    \begin{itemize}
      \item Carried out by White and Black people
    \end{itemize}
  \end{itemize}
\end{frame}